The \LaTeX\ package BibBreeze, written using \LaTeX3, is a referencing
package that automates bibliography reconstruction, eliminating manual
effort in reference handling. It reorders disorganized fields for
bibliography entries, fills in missing fields, and produces polished,
reference style-compliant bibliographies optimized for researchers,
academics, and writers. Currently, the package's referencing style is
designed for APA, both \verb|numeric| and \verb|authoryear| in-text
citations, with more styles to come.\par

Using powerful packages such as \verb|expl3| and fundamental features
such as \verb|regex|, BibBreeze\ automatically extracts essential
information from bibliography (\BibTeX) entries and formats it according
to the referencing guidelines. Furthermore, it distinguishes between
entry subtypes such as proceedings papers (presented, published in
journals or books) all identified by \verb|@inproceedings|, using
targeted checks. These features are especially valuable for users
managing large reference lists who need precise formatting.
